Article 14 For the filing of Class I medical device products and the application for registration of Class II and Class III medical device products, the following materials shall be submitted:
(1) Product risk analysis materials;
(2) Product technical requirements;
(3) Product inspection reports;
(4) Clinical evaluation materials;
(5) Product instructions and label samples;
(6) Quality management system documents related to product research, development, and production;
(7) Other materials necessary to demonstrate the safety and effectiveness of the product.
Product inspection reports shall comply with the requirements of the drug regulatory department of the State Council, and may be self-inspection reports of the medical device registration applicant or filing person, or inspection reports issued by a qualified medical device inspection institution commissioned by them.
Where the circumstances exempting from clinical evaluation as prescribed in Article 24 of these Regulations are met, the clinical evaluation materials may be exempted from submission.
Medical device registration applicants and filing persons shall ensure that the submitted materials are lawful, true, accurate, complete, and traceable.

Article 20 Medical device registrants and filing persons shall perform the following obligations:
(1) Establish a quality management system appropriate to the product and maintain its effective operation;
(2) Formulate post-market research and risk management and control plans and ensure their effective implementation;
(3) Carry out adverse event monitoring and re-evaluation in accordance with law;
(4) Establish and implement a product traceability and recall system;
(5) Other obligations prescribed by the drug regulatory department of the State Council.
The enterprise legal person within the territory of China designated by an overseas medical device registrant or filing person shall assist the registrant or filing person in performing the obligations specified in the preceding paragraph.

Article 22 The term of validity of a medical device registration certificate shall be five years. Where renewal of registration is required upon expiration of the term of validity, an application for renewal of registration shall be submitted to the original registration authority six months prior to the expiration of the term of validity.
Except as provided in the third paragraph of this Article, the medical product regulatory authority that receives the application for renewal of registration shall make a decision to approve the renewal before the expiration of the term of validity of the medical device registration certificate. If no decision is made within the time limit, the renewal shall be deemed to have been approved.
In any of the following circumstances, renewal of registration shall not be granted:
(1) The application for renewal of registration is not submitted within the prescribed time limit;
(2) The mandatory standards for medical devices have been revised, and the medical device for which renewal of registration is applied fails to meet the new requirements;
(3) For a medical device approved under conditions, the matters specified in the medical device registration certificate are not completed within the prescribed time limit.

Article 30 To engage in the production of medical devices, the following conditions shall be met:
(1) Having production sites, environmental conditions, production equipment and professional technical personnel suitable for the medical devices produced;
(2) Having an institution or full-time inspection personnel capable of performing quality inspection on the produced medical devices, as well as inspection equipment;
(3) Having a management system to ensure the quality of medical devices;
(4) Having after-sales service capability suitable for the medical devices produced;
(5) Meeting the requirements specified in the product development and production process documents.

Article 39 A medical device shall have an instruction manual and a label. The contents of the instruction manual and label shall be consistent with the relevant registered or filed contents, and be true and accurate.
The instruction manual and label of a medical device shall indicate the following items:
(1) Common name, model, and specification;
(2) Name, address and contact information of the medical device registrant, filer or entrusted production enterprise;
(3) Date of manufacture, use period or expiry date;
(4) Product performance, main structure, and scope of application;
(5) Contraindications, precautions and other content requiring warnings or prompts;
(6) Installation and use instructions or diagrams;
(7) Maintenance and care methods, special transport and storage conditions and methods;
(8) Other content that shall be indicated as specified by product technical requirements.
A Class II or Class III medical device shall also indicate the number of the medical device registration certificate.
A medical device intended for self-use by individual consumers shall also include special instructions for safe use.

Article 45 A medical device operation enterprise or using unit shall purchase medical devices from a medical device registrant, filing person, or production or operation enterprise with lawful qualifications. When purchasing medical devices, it shall check the qualifications of the supplier and the certificate of conformity of the medical devices, and establish a system of records for incoming inspection. An operation enterprise engaged in the wholesale business of Class II and Class III medical devices or the retail business of Class III medical devices shall also establish a system of sales records.
The record items include:
(1) the name, model, specification and quantity of the medical device;
(2) the production batch number, use period or expiry date, and sale date of the medical device;
(3) the names of the medical device registrant, filing person and entrusted production enterprise;
(4) the name, address and contact information of the supplier or purchaser;
(5) the numbers of relevant license certificate documents, etc.
The incoming inspection records and sales records shall be authentic, accurate, complete and traceable, and shall be kept within the period prescribed by the drug administration department under the State Council. The State encourages the use of advanced technical means for recording.

Article 69 The drug regulatory department shall strengthen supervision and inspection of the research and development, production, and operation activities of medical devices as well as the quality of medical devices in the use stage, and shall conduct key supervision and inspection on the following matters:
(1) whether production is organized in accordance with the product technical requirements approved upon registration or recorded;
(2) whether the quality management system remains effectively operational;
(3) whether production and operation conditions continuously meet the statutory requirements.
Where necessary, the drug regulatory department may carry out extended inspections on other relevant entities or individuals that provide products or services for activities such as research and development, production, operation, and use of medical devices.

Article 70 The drug regulatory department shall have the following powers in conducting supervision and inspection:
(1) entering the site to carry out inspections and take samples;
(2) reviewing, copying, sealing, and seizing relevant contracts, invoices, account books, and other relevant materials;
(3) sealing and seizing medical devices that do not meet statutory requirements, illegally used spare parts and raw materials, as well as tools and equipment used for illegally producing or operating medical devices;
(4) sealing premises where medical device production or operation activities are carried out in violation of these Regulations.
When conducting supervision and inspection, law enforcement documents shall be presented, and the trade secrets of the inspected entity shall be kept confidential.
Relevant entities and individuals shall cooperate with the supervision and inspection, provide relevant documents and materials, and shall not conceal, refuse, or obstruct.

Article 81 In any of the following circumstances, the drug regulatory authority shall confiscate the illegal gains, the medical devices illegally produced or operated, and the tools, equipment, raw materials, and other articles used for such illegal production or operation; if the value of the illegally produced or operated medical devices is less than RMB 10,000 Yuan, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 Yuan but not more than RMB 150,000 Yuan shall also be imposed; if the value is RMB 10,000 Yuan or more, a fine of not less than 15 times but not more than 30 times the value of the goods shall also be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the production or business operation shall be ordered to suspend for rectification, no application for a medical device license submitted by the relevant responsible persons and the entity shall be accepted within 10 years, and the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor and other responsible persons of the illegal entity shall have their income obtained from the entity during the period when the illegal act occurred confiscated, and a fine of not less than 30% but not more than 3 times the income obtained shall also be imposed, and they shall be permanently prohibited from engaging in the production or operation of medical devices:
(1) producing or operating Class II or Class III medical devices without obtaining a medical device registration certificate;
(2) engaging in the production of Class II or Class III medical devices without a license;
(3) engaging in the operation of Class III medical devices without a license.
If the circumstance under item (1) of the preceding paragraph is serious, the original issuing authority shall revoke the medical device production license or the medical device operation license.

Article 84 In any of the following circumstances, the drug regulatory authority shall announce the name of the entity and the product to the public and order rectification within a prescribed time limit; if no rectification is made upon expiry of the time limit, the illegal gains and the medical devices illegally produced or operated shall be confiscated; if the value of the illegally produced or operated medical devices is less than RMB 10,000 Yuan, a fine of not less than RMB 10,000 Yuan but not more than RMB 50,000 Yuan shall also be imposed; if the value is RMB 10,000 Yuan or more, a fine of not less than 5 times but not more than 20 times the value of the goods shall also be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor and other responsible persons of the illegal entity shall have their income obtained from the entity during the period when the illegal act occurred confiscated, a fine of not less than 30% but not more than 2 times the income obtained shall also be imposed, and they shall be prohibited from engaging in the production or operation of medical devices for 5 years:
(1) producing or operating Class I medical devices that have not been filed;
(2) engaging in the production of Class I medical devices without filing;
(3) operating Class II medical devices that should be filed but are not filed;
(4) the filed materials do not meet the requirements.

Article 86 In any of the following circumstances, the drug regulatory authority shall order rectification and confiscate the medical devices illegally produced, operated or used; if the value of the illegally produced, operated or used medical devices is less than RMB 10,000 Yuan, a fine of not less than RMB 20,000 Yuan but not more than RMB 50,000 Yuan shall also be imposed; if the value is RMB 10,000 Yuan or more, a fine of not less than 5 times but not more than 20 times the value of the goods shall also be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the production or business operation shall be ordered to suspend for rectification until the original issuing authority revokes the medical device registration certificate, medical device production license, or medical device operation license, and the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor and other responsible persons of the illegal entity shall have their income obtained from the entity during the period when the illegal act occurred confiscated, a fine of not less than 30% but not more than 3 times the income obtained shall also be imposed, and they shall be prohibited from engaging in the production or operation of medical devices for 10 years:
(1) producing, operating or using medical devices that do not meet mandatory standards or do not meet the product technical requirements approved or filed;
(2) failing to organize production in accordance with the product technical requirements approved or filed, or failing to establish and maintain effective operation of a quality management system in accordance with these Regulations, affecting product safety and efficacy;
(3) operating or using medical devices without certificate of conformity, expired, invalid, eliminated, or using medical devices that are not registered according to law;
(4) refusing to recall after being ordered to recall by the drug regulatory authority, or refusing to stop production, import or operation after being ordered to stop or suspend production, import or operation;
(5) entrusting an enterprise that does not meet the conditions prescribed in these Regulations to produce medical devices, or failing to manage the production activities of the entrusted enterprise;
(6) importing expired, invalid, eliminated or other used medical devices.

Article 88 In any of the following circumstances, the drug regulatory authority shall order rectification and impose a fine of not less than RMB 10,000 Yuan but not more than RMB 50,000 Yuan; if no rectification is made, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 Yuan but not more than RMB 100,000 Yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the production or business operation shall be ordered to suspend for rectification until the original issuing authority revokes the medical device production license or medical device operation license, and the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor and other responsible persons of the illegal entity shall have their income obtained from the entity during the period when the illegal act occurred confiscated, a fine of not less than 30% but not more than 2 times the income obtained shall also be imposed, and they shall be prohibited from engaging in the production or operation of medical devices for 5 years:
(1) the production conditions change and no longer meet the requirements of the medical device quality management system, and the entity fails to rectify, stop production or report in accordance with these Regulations;
(2) producing or operating medical devices whose instructions or labels do not comply with these Regulations;
(3) failing to transport or store medical devices in accordance with the requirements indicated in the instructions and labels of the medical devices;
(4) transferring used medical devices that are expired, invalid, eliminated or fail inspection.

Article 89 In any of the following circumstances, the drug regulatory authority and the health authority shall, within their respective duties, order rectification and give a warning; if no rectification is made, a fine of not less than RMB 10,000 Yuan but not more than RMB 100,000 Yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, the production or business operation shall be ordered to suspend for rectification until the original issuing authority revokes the medical device registration certificate, medical device production license, or medical device operation license, and a fine of not less than RMB 10,000 Yuan but not more than RMB 30,000 Yuan shall be imposed on the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor and other responsible persons of the illegal entity:
(1) failing to submit a self-inspection report on the quality management system as required;
(2) purchasing medical devices from a supplier without lawful qualifications;
(3) a medical device business enterprise or user fails to establish and implement a record system for incoming inspection of medical devices in accordance with these Regulations;
(4) a business enterprise engaged in wholesale of Class II or Class III medical devices or retail of Class III medical devices fails to establish and implement a sales record system in accordance with these Regulations;
(5) a medical device registrant, filer, production or business enterprise, or user fails to carry out adverse event monitoring for medical devices in accordance with these Regulations, fails to report adverse events as required, or fails to cooperate with the adverse event investigation conducted by the medical device adverse event monitoring technical institution, the drug regulatory authority, or the health authority;
(6) a medical device registrant or filer fails to formulate a post-marketing research and risk control plan and ensure its effective implementation as required;
(7) a medical device registrant or filer fails to establish and implement a product traceability system as required;
(8) a medical device registrant, filer or business enterprise engaging in online sales of medical devices fails to inform the drug regulatory authority as required;
(9) for medical devices that require periodic inspection, testing, calibration, maintenance or servicing, a medical device user fails to carry out inspection, testing, calibration, maintenance or servicing and keep records in accordance with the product instructions, and analyze and assess in a timely manner to ensure the medical devices are in good condition;
(10) a medical device user fails to properly keep the original materials of purchased Class III medical devices.

Article 90 In any of the following circumstances, the health authority of the people's government at or above the county level shall order rectification and give a warning; if no rectification is made, a fine of not less than RMB 50,000 Yuan but not more than RMB 100,000 Yuan shall be imposed; if the circumstances are serious, a fine of not less than RMB 100,000 Yuan but not more than RMB 300,000 Yuan shall be imposed, order suspension of the relevant medical device use activities until the original issuing authority revokes the practice license, order the relevant responsible persons to suspend practice for not less than 6 months but not more than 1 year according to law, until the original issuing authority revokes the practice certificates of the relevant persons, and the legal representative, principal responsible person, directly responsible supervisor and other responsible persons of the illegal entity shall have their income obtained from the entity during the period when the illegal act occurred confiscated, a fine of not less than 30% but not more than 3 times the income obtained shall also be imposed, and sanctions shall be imposed according to law:
(1) for reusable medical devices, a medical device user fails to process them in accordance with the disinfection and management requirements;
(2) a medical device user reuses single-use medical devices, or fails to destroy used single-use medical devices as required;
(3) a medical device user fails to record information on large-scale medical devices and implantable or interventional medical devices in medical records or other relevant records as required;
(4) a medical device user discovers that a medical device in use has a safety hazard but fails to immediately stop use, notify for repair, or continues to use a medical device that after repair still cannot meet the safety standards for use;
(5) a medical device user uses large-scale medical equipment in violation of regulations, failing to ensure medical quality and safety.

Article 103 For the purposes of these Regulations, the meanings of the following terms are as defined below:
Medical devices refer to instruments, equipment, appliances, in vitro diagnostic reagents and calibrators, materials, and other similar or related items intended for use in humans directly or indirectly, including the necessary computer software; their effects are mainly achieved through physical means, etc., and not through pharmacological, immunological, or metabolic means, or, even if such means are involved, they play only an auxiliary role; and their purposes are:
(1) diagnosis, prevention, monitoring, treatment, or alleviation of diseases;
(2) diagnosis, monitoring, treatment, alleviation, or functional compensation of injuries;
(3) examination, replacement, adjustment, or support of physiological structures or processes;
(4) support or maintenance of life;
(5) control of pregnancy;
(6) providing information for medical or diagnostic purposes through the examination of human body samples.
Medical device registrant or filing person means an enterprise or research institution that has obtained a medical device registration certificate or has completed a medical device filing.
Medical device using unit means an institution that uses medical devices to provide medical or other technical services to others, including medical institutions, blood stations, plasma collection stations, rehabilitation assistive device fitting agencies, etc.
Large-scale medical equipment means large medical devices that are technically complex, require a large capital investment, have high operating costs, have a significant impact on medical expenses, and are included in directory management.
